-- (1) CORRECTNESS: acquire every affected topics row lock up front, ONE -- ROW AT A TIME via a single-table, PK-indexed, join-free `FOR UPDATE` -- — see the IMPLEMENTATION NOTE above for why a JOIN-based `ORDER BY -- ... FOR UPDATE` does NOT reliably serialize this (PostgreSQL's -- LockRows node locks in JOIN order, not sorted order, once a join is -- involved). Iterating the PRE-SORTED arrays above one indexed -- single-row lock at a time is what actually guarantees every -- concurrent invocation acquires the shared topics in the same -- relative order. FOR v_i IN 1 .. COALESCE(array_length(v_topic_ids, 1), 0) LOOP PERFORM 1 FROM nexus.topics WHERE tenant_id = v_tenant_ids[v_i] AND id = v_topic_ids[v_i] FOR UPDATE; END LOOP;
